{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists","id":1050234,"title":"How would you do Hackers as antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T19:08:05-08:00","id":1050234,"title":"How would you do Hackers as antagonists?","content":"I thought up a new villain. They are a group of hackers called the Grinning Skulls who are either sponsored by a Abyssal or a Lich. How could this work in Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:13:59-08:00","id":1050236,"title":"","content":"Mystery Cult merit with specialties in hacking and appropriate supernatural merit granted by sponsor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:31:38-08:00","id":1050249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1050236#post1050236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mystery Cult merit with specialties in hacking and appropriate supernatural merit granted by sponsor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. How do you think I could do the whole Mage Vs. Hackers thing and have it make sense in the game's setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:38:00-08:00","id":1050256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1050249#post1050249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. How do you think I could do the whole Mage Vs. Hackers thing and have it make sense in the game's setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well anything digital is something they could screw with, if a PC owns a business they could wreak the reputation or even get them in trouble with the law. Gotta remember mages are people first sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:41:20-08:00","id":1050260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1050256#post1050256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well anything digital is something they could screw with, if a PC owns a business they could wreak the reputation or even get them in trouble with the law. Gotta remember mages are people first sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could also hack into a chantry which has a computer and sell the information to Banishers. I am also wondering which Order would fight them the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:46:13-08:00","id":1050264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1050260#post1050260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could also hack into a chantry which has a computer and sell the information to Banishers. I am also wondering which Order would fight them the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably do some research on actual cyber security before you go crazy. It's not anything like on t.v. They would have to somehow get access to the computer through malware or social engineering. <br /> <br /> I would guess the free Council or an arrow who specializes in cyber warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T21:41:52-08:00","id":1050318,"title":"","content":"Is it really a case of hackers going against Mages, or is it hackers engaged in some nefarious plot that will run afoul of said Mages?<br /> \u200bIf it's the later than the Chronicle is more likely to be about the Mages trying to undue whatever the hackers did before they got involved.<br /> \u200bEither way the hackers have two things in their favor; anonymity and distance.<br /> \u200bBacked by an Abyssal or Mage finding the hackers and acting against them directly won't be easy, after all they can attack from anywhere there is a Wi-Fi hot spot and their attacks won't be direct either, they can bury your characters under unrelated distractions from arrest warrants to family services dropping by to investigate an anonymous tip. The goal being to keep the Mages so busy reacting that they can't act or strike back.<br /> \u200bThe real question is what are the hackers trying to achieve, and are the Mages the target or just an obstacle?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:06:48-08:00","id":1050532,"title":"","content":"The actual mechanics (both in narrative and game terms) are not that relevant. What you have to keep in mind is what are hackers good at, and that's getting information. What information could harm the Mages if it fell on thw wrong hands? How? Why? Who are these wrong hands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:59:05-08:00","id":1050819,"title":"","content":"I guess information about their chantries could harm them. Also, I have no idea about their goals yet but the mages would most likely be an obstacle. Also, would these guys be considered a Mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:15:41-08:00","id":1050845,"title":"","content":"They'd only be a Mystery for their supernatural component and only till Mages figure that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:02:53-08:00","id":1050952,"title":"","content":"Lets start at the top, shall we? Mage revolves three central themes. War for reality/humanity's destiny. Mysteries and Obsessions. Hubris. Everything comes back to these three. Now, here's my first question:<br /> <br /> ~ What are these hackers supposed to tie into? Are they basically hactivist hunters that can't tell Assembly, Diamond and Seer apart, and want to bring down the Awakened from controlling people? Do they represent a mystery to study or are they protecting a mystery? I'm not really sure how this ties into a game's themes.<br /> <br /> ~ Its trivially easy for a mage with a touch of Forces and Space to trace the hackers back through sympathetic connections. It gets even easier if actual supernatural power is involved. Hackers generally need to be invivisible to be effective. How are they handled?<br /> <br /> ~ Why are the PCs being targetted?<br /> <br /> ~ Do these guys necessarily need to be antagonists? Are they completely black hats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:16:00-08:00","id":1051044,"title":"","content":"For goals:<br /> If the hackers are servants of the Abyss then maybe they are spreading its anti-truth through virtual reality, people sit down at their computers and find themselves downloading the Abyss.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf something along the line of hunters maybe they aren't the ones attacking, instead they are identifying Mages (or possible Mages) by tracking internet activity, then gathering information used by others to perform real attacks.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe the hackers are Mages. There was at least one Legacy based on using the Cloud (or something like it) to exploit Sleepers.<br /> How about the hackers being the first prong of a Seer offensive, a non supernal attack meant to handicap the Pentacle in an area without setting off the normal magic sensing alarms.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe hackers know nothing of Mages but they have cottoned onto the effects of Resonance and now they are experimenting with it, manipulating it through the flow of information. They could certainly raise clouds of paranoia and insecurity. Think cyber-terrorism, fear doesn't have to include physical death sometimes having your whole life gutted by strangers is enough.<br /> <br /> Maybe they are something else, something that has raised identity theft to a whole new level, one that includes your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:56:58-08:00","id":1051134,"title":"","content":"Well, they are servants of the Abyss so the spreading the Abyss by downloads is pretty good. I am not sure about how they could combat mage but they could use Resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:06:12-08:00","id":1051168,"title":"","content":"Something something Nemesis Continuum running calculations on infected &quot;zombie&quot; machines, something?<br /> <br /> As for combating Mage &quot;I See You&quot;, maybe part of the effect/corruption is that each proxy acts as another link in the sympathetic chain? Mage follows the trail... to a server in China, then one in Brazil, then one in... etc. Make it too tiresome to follow the links.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:35:44-08:00","id":1051357,"title":"","content":"Do the &quot;Ghost in the Machine&quot; bit, where each hacker they find turns out to be just another victim, links in a long chain to a virtual body jumping entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:54:36-08:00","id":1051407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1051357#post1051357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the &quot;Ghost in the Machine&quot; bit, where each hacker they find turns out to be just another victim, links in a long chain to a virtual body jumping entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>this could be supported by the &quot;virtual talented&quot; Body Thieves from Immortals- but maybe instead of having other people jumping from one body to another it is some sort of an abyssal entity which traps their souls in computers ad downloads copies of themselves into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T16:29:15-08:00","id":1051740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050234-how-would-you-do-hackers-as-antagonists?p=1051357#post1051357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the &quot;Ghost in the Machine&quot; bit, where each hacker they find turns out to be just another victim, links in a long chain to a virtual body jumping entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can picture a scene with the Mages breaking down a door in some hacker's basement only to find him dead. Then suddenly, someone starts to shot at them from outside the house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}